WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.568
-Hi, everyone.
Thanks for tuning in.

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:04.170
My name is Jimmy Fallon.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.538
And hi, Roots.
Nice to see you.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.672
Very nice.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:08.841
-Hey, hey.
-Quest, you -- you made it --

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:10.576
you made it into the studio
today, which --

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:11.577
-Good. I escaped.

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:12.912
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.314
-What, were you in between
two trees or where --

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:18.685
-I was in between -- I was on
the set of "Jumanji."

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.919
That's where I was.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.919 --> 00:00:23.256
-Did you know -- I mean,
did you get out of your vehicle

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.325
and walk home?
-I ran home.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.592
Yes.
-Yeah.

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:28.461
-Trees, power lines,
everything was falling.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.597
Turkeys in the street.
Bears on the corner.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.899
Deer everywhere.
Like --

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.034
-Oh, my gosh.
-Yesterday was all --

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:36.503
[ Singing theme ]

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:38.337
-Yeah, it was all crazy, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:39.806
-Well, welcome back.
Thanks for --

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:42.709
Thanks for being here.
I mean, I am happy you're here.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.443
-Well, thank you.
Glad to be here.

00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:47.012
-I mean, thankful
but also happy.

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:49.482
-I'm grateful
and thankful that you're happy.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.217
-There you go. Good.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.887
Well, I mean, same goes with
you, Tariq, as well.

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:56.790
-I appreciate that.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:57.991
-Yeah.

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:02.161
James.
Nice to see you.

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.030
-Ooshi, ooshi.
-Ooshi.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.032
Let's get to the news.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.933
Let's get to some jokes here,
guys.

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:10.836
After the nightmare that was
his interview on HBO,

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:13.406
this morning President Trump
cocooned himself

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.875
in the weighted blanket
that is "Fox &amp; Friends."

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.077
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.580
That's right.
After several brutal interviews,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.182
Trump called in to
"Fox &amp; Friends" this morning.

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:25.785
He basically tried dating
other shows and then ended up

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:28.454
back with his ex.
"Well, well, well.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:30.857
Look who came crawling back."

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:35.128
Yep. Trump went on and on this
morning for 53 minutes.

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:37.129
Most Americans were like,
"Hey, if we wanted to hear

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:38.764
the President ramble
about nothing for an hour,

00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:40.633
we'd have watched the
coronavirus briefing."

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.435
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.869
The interview with
"Fox &amp; Friends" went about

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:45.204
how you would expect.

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.306
At one point, Trump made a
pretty shocking claim

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:49.842
about how long mail-in
voting could delay the results

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.610
of the election.
Listen to this.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.746 line:0%
-If it doesn't work out,
you're not going to know

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:55.715 line:0%
the November 3rd
election results.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.216 line:0%
I'm talking for the country.

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:59.152 line:0%
It could be for months
and months.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.120 line:0%
I mean, actually,
it could be for years.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.723
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.391
-Months or years?

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:08.094
It's an election, not the
results of a COVID test.

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:10.096
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:12.365
Yeah, Trump was like,
"It's going to take a while.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:14.734
Imagine the time it takes me
to walk down a ramp.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.269
Now double that.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.805
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.642
I was wearing wooden --

00:02:23.642 --> 00:02:24.977
[ Laughs ]

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:27.746
I was wearing wooden soled
shoes, or leather soled.

00:02:27.746 --> 00:02:30.015
Brand new, made from wood.
They were wooden.

00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:32.985
I was wearing clogs."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:35.254
At one point, Trump was asked
about schools reopening

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:37.056
and here's what he had
to say.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.924
-My view is the
schools should open.

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:40.994
This thing is going away.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:44.297
It will go away
like things go away.

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:46.733
And my view is that schools
should be open.

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:49.602
If you look at children,
children are almost --

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.804
and I would almost say
definitely --

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.506
but almost immune
from this disease.

00:02:54.506 --> 00:02:57.776
[ Crew groans ]

00:02:57.776 --> 00:03:01.047
-"For example, I've had people
coughing on Don Jr.'s face

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.749
for months,
and so far nothing."

00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:06.152
At that point, Dr. Birx wrapped
her scarf around her eyes

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.754
and just walked into traffic.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.555
She's like, "I --"

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:12.692
Even Brian Kilmeade seems to be
losing faith in Trump,

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.827
because after that,
he poured out a Diet Coke

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:18.096
and sang "It's So Hard to Say
Goodbye (To Yesterday)."

00:03:18.096 --> 00:03:20.532
It was such a bad answer,
for the rest of the interview,

00:03:20.532 --> 00:03:23.636
"Fox &amp; Friends" replaced
all the anchors with this.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.538
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.439
Yeah, a lot of people are
criticizing the interview,

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:28.808
but Trump was proud of it.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:31.443
Right after, he held up a chart
showing that the U.S.

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:34.280
leads the world in calls
into morning shows.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.949
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:39.518
"You can see it right here.
It's very clear."

00:03:39.518 --> 00:03:41.320
Later in the interview,
Trump was asked about

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.689
his convention speech and where
it will take place.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:44.991
Listen to what he had to say.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.893
-There are reports
that you're considering

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:50.129
possibly giving your
convention acceptance speech

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.764
from the White House lawn.

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:54.133
Well, we're thinking about it.
It would be the easiest

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.801
from the standpoint of security.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:58.337
It's easy. And I think
it's a beautiful setting.

00:03:58.337 --> 00:04:01.174
I love the building.
I'm there right now.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.742
I spend a lot of time here.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.376
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.376 --> 00:04:06.546
-Yeah, Trump was like, "Where
are they going to have it?

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:10.083
At the White House or
Yo-se-Mite National Park."

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.719
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:15.655
"Or the banks of
the Mis-pee-pee River."

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:16.889
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:19.025
"I'm still deciding."
That's for you, Robin.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.793
Basically Trump's message is,

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.861
"Nobody should worry
about the virus.

00:04:22.861 --> 00:04:24.697
Anyway, totally unrelated,

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.365
I'll be giving my speech
from home."

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:28.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.236
Meanwhile when Trump said it
would be easier for security,

00:04:31.236 --> 00:04:34.039
the Secret Service
was like, "Yeah, we're good.

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:36.943
I think we can handle it.
Don't worry about it."

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.377
But Trump's not the only one
who's changing

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:39.912
his convention plans.
Watch.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.080 line:0%
-Breaking news from

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.749 line:0%
the Democratic National
Campaign Committee

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.984 line:0%
announcing that former
Vice President Joe Biden

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.719 line:0%
will not be traveling
to Milwaukee,

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:50.822 line:0%
a battleground state, Wisconsin,
due to concerns over COVID-19.

00:04:50.822 --> 00:04:54.560 line:0%
Instead, Biden will accept the
nomination from Delaware.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.329
-Right now in Milwaukee, the guy
who just blew up 10,000 balloons

00:04:57.329 --> 00:04:59.932
is like, [ High-pitched ]
"Are you fricking kidding me?"

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:04.103
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:06.305
Biden says he wants to speak
in front of Delaware's

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:08.140
most famous landmark,
the sign that says,

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.642
"Welcome to Pennsylvania."

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:12.511
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:14.113
Well, guys, get this.
In --

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:18.617
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:20.919
Guys, get this,
a new poll found that

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:23.355
four out of five parents have
considered home schooling

00:05:23.355 --> 00:05:25.024
their kids this fall.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:26.959
To hear from the other side,
we're now joined by

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:30.363
one of the parents who hasn't
considered home schooling.

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:32.632 line:0%
Hey, thanks for joining us.

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:34.033 line:0%
-Hey.

00:05:36.735 --> 00:05:39.839
-So like I said, most parents
are at least thinking

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:41.640
about home schooling
their kids this fall,

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.276
but you're not.

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:44.944
-Nope.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.849
-You haven't even
thought about it?

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:51.250
-Nope.

00:05:53.118 --> 00:05:55.454
-I mean, if there was a major
outbreak in your area,

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:57.857
you'd consider it,
though, right?

00:05:57.857 --> 00:05:58.925
-Nope.

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:02.227
-What if health officials
advised you

00:06:02.227 --> 00:06:04.731
to home school your kids?

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:06.866
-Nope.

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:09.735
-Okay, but, let's say schools
are fully closed this fall.

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:13.139
You have no choice but to
home school your kids, right?

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:15.107
-Debatable.

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:17.242
-I mean, you wouldn't just
drop them off in a parking lot

00:06:17.242 --> 00:06:19.712
in an empty school.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:22.482
-Maybe.

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:24.650
-How many kids do you have?

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.753
-Seven.

00:06:26.753 --> 00:06:28.520
-Wow.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:29.988
How old are they?

00:06:29.988 --> 00:06:32.425
-12.

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:36.728
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.728 --> 00:06:39.232
-All of your kids are 12?

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:41.400
-Yep.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.970
-How many boys?
How many girls?

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.805
-Boys.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:47.639
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.639 --> 00:06:49.809
-All boys?

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:51.577
-Yep.

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:53.513
-So you've been in a house
all summer

00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:56.649
with seven 12-year-old boys?

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:57.783
-Yep.

00:06:57.783 --> 00:06:59.852
[ Knocking sound ]

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:01.120
Jesus.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.488
[ Knocking ]

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:04.223
-I'm sorry, wait --
-[ Boys shouting ]

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:08.060
-Are you -- are you doing this
interview from your bathroom?

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.062
-Yep.
-[ Shouting continues ]

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:11.898
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:14.834
-Is it the only place
you can be alone?

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:15.868
-Yep.

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:18.103
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.103 --> 00:07:19.204
[ Knocking continues ]

00:07:19.204 --> 00:07:21.541
-Do you work out of there, too?

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:23.842
-Yep.

00:07:23.842 --> 00:07:25.177
-What do you do
for a living?

00:07:25.177 --> 00:07:26.678
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.678 --> 00:07:28.981
-Air traffic control.

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:30.582
-I'll let you get back
to work then.

00:07:30.582 --> 00:07:32.752
The parent who hasn't considered
home schooling, everyone.

00:07:32.752 --> 00:07:36.322
[ Applause ]

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:38.624
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.624 --> 00:07:41.527
-The loop.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:43.696
Can I just hear
the loop one more time?

00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:46.531
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.531 --> 00:07:48.767
[ Imitates knock ]
[ Knocking ]

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:50.202
-Let's get to some
entertainment news.

00:07:50.202 --> 00:07:52.805
Guys, earlier today, Disney made
a big announcement.

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:56.075 line:0%
-After months of delays,
audiences will finally be able

00:07:56.075 --> 00:07:58.677 line:0%
to see Disney's
live action "Mulan" at home.

00:07:58.677 --> 00:08:01.613 line:0%
The remake of the classic is
heading to Disney+

00:08:01.613 --> 00:08:04.850 line:0%
on September 4th
for an additional $30.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:08.020
-Yeah. "Mulan" will be
on Disney+ for 30 bucks.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.188
That is why when you click
purchase, it says,

00:08:10.188 --> 00:08:11.890
"Are you sure?"
Then is says,

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.859
"Seriously, are you sure?"
Then, finally, it says,

00:08:13.859 --> 00:08:15.328
"Okay, Rockefeller."

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:17.463
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.463 --> 00:08:19.365
30 bucks may seem like a lot,
but remember,

00:08:19.365 --> 00:08:21.734
if you took your kid to the
theater, your tickets are $20,

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:23.736
the snacks are $10,
and you haven't even gotten to

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:26.505
the vodka Red Bull
in your hydro flask.

00:08:26.505 --> 00:08:28.340
Well, guys, with everything
that's happening,

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:30.376
it's also a big week for
celebrity birthdays.

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:32.211
President Obama,
Billy Bob Thornton,

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:34.479
Tony Bennett,
Arnold Schwarzenegger.

00:08:34.479 --> 00:08:35.715
So, we thought it would be fun
to take a break

00:08:35.715 --> 00:08:37.349
from all the news
and imagine them

00:08:37.349 --> 00:08:39.118
all in a room together just
wishing each other

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:41.153
happy birthday.
Take a look.

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:43.689
-Happy birthday, Billy.
-Happy birthday, Barack.

00:08:43.689 --> 00:08:46.859
-Happy birthday, Arnold.
-Happy birthday, Tony.

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:49.695
-Happy b-day, Barack.
-Happy birthday, Tony.

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:50.829
-Happy birthday, Billy.

00:08:50.829 --> 00:08:52.097
-Happy birthday, Arnold.

00:08:52.097 --> 00:08:53.498
-Happy birthday, Billy.

00:08:53.498 --> 00:08:54.833
-Happy birthday, Tony.

00:08:54.833 --> 00:08:57.036
-Happy birthday, Arnold.
-Happy birthday, Barack.

00:08:57.036 --> 00:08:58.838
-Okay.
Happy birthday on three.

00:08:58.838 --> 00:09:00.373
One, two, three!

00:09:00.373 --> 00:09:02.041
-Happy birthday!

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:03.275
-Where's the cake?

00:09:03.275 --> 00:09:06.545
[ Laughter ]

00:09:06.545 --> 00:09:08.481
-[ As Tony Bennett ]
"Happy birthday."

00:09:08.481 --> 00:09:12.451
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:14.620
That's the best one.
-I know.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.522
-And finally,
this is crazy.

00:09:16.522 --> 00:09:19.558
Three men were stranded on a
deserted island in the Pacific,

00:09:19.558 --> 00:09:21.627
so they drew a giant "SOS"
on the beach

00:09:21.627 --> 00:09:24.296
and it actually worked.
Yep.

00:09:24.296 --> 00:09:26.331
They got rescued by a helicopter
after just three days.

00:09:26.331 --> 00:09:27.766
Check it out.

00:09:27.766 --> 00:09:29.134
See that?
Yeah.

00:09:29.134 --> 00:09:30.802
Asked how they survived,
they said,

00:09:30.802 --> 00:09:33.172
"Well, let's just say there
used to be four of us."

00:09:33.172 --> 00:09:35.041
[ Laughter ]

